"""Template for dourmouse/_builtin_oauth.py — the product's ONE shared
Google OAuth client, for a commercially distributed build where end
users should need zero Google Cloud Console setup of their own.

This file itself IS committed (a template, no real values). The real
dourmouse/_builtin_oauth.py is gitignored — see google_auth.py's own
comment on _builtin_oauth() for why a real, working credential never
belongs in this repo's public history, even though Google's OAuth docs
say a "Desktop app" client secret is not meant to be treated as truly
confidential.

To wire the real shared client:
  1. Google Cloud Console -> APIs & Services -> Credentials ->
     Create Credentials -> OAuth client ID -> "Desktop app" (NOT "Web
     application" — Desktop app auto-permits localhost/127.0.0.1 on
     any port, so this dynamically-resolved redirect_uri never hits a
     redirect_uri_mismatch as ports vary across installs).
  2. Copy this file to dourmouse/_builtin_oauth.py (same directory,
     drop the .example suffix).
  3. Fill in the two real values below.
  4. Every install of this app now offers "Sign in with Google" with
     no per-user Google Cloud project required — an env var
     (GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID/GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET) still overrides this for
     a power user who wants their own client instead.
"""

GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID = ""
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET = ""
